<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Cusco</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Cuzco, Qosqo</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Cusco is a city in the Andes of southern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/peru">Peru</a>, about 3,400 metres above sea level, which was the capital of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/inca-empire">Inca Empire</a>. Its palaces and temples, including the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coricancha">Coricancha</a>, were rebuilt by the Spaniards after 1533 on Inca foundations, and the fortress-shrine of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sacsayhuaman">Sacsayhuamán</a> stands above it. The city is a World Heritage Site.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/cusco.jpg" alt="Cusco" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: tomscoffin · CC BY 2.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Vista_Calle_Suecia.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
